$ but less than $6.$ So,\n\n$$\nA={1,2,3,4,5}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are natural numbers which satisfy the inequality $3x<9.$ So,\n\n$$\nB={1,2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊆B$ is false, while $A⊈B$ is true. For example, $5\\in A$ but $5\\notin B.$\n\n- $B⊆A$ is true. Every element in the set $B$ is an element of the set $A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." 13194139535885 true] [17592186372602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372603 13194139535885 true] [17592186372602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372604 13194139535885 true] [17592186372602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372605 13194139535885 true] [17592186372602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372606 13194139535885 true] [17592186372602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372607 13194139535885 true] [17592186372602 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535885 true] [17592186372602 1041 "selection" 13194139535885 true] [17592186372602 1104 #edb/ref 17592186372603 13194139535885 true] [17592186372602 1110 #uuid "8d8700e1-65a3-5893-ba8a-9a9dea1279f5" 13194139535885 true] [17592186372603 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535885 true] [17592186372603 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535885 true] [17592186372603 1111 #uuid "b2a9ab72-020d-5396-8333-01a81f55d78f" 13194139535885 true] [17592186372604 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535885 true] [17592186372604 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535885 true] [17592186372604 1111 #uuid "48e4bf35-5c06-5b1c-8696-11f535bda248" 13194139535885 true] [17592186372605 1034 "I only" 13194139535885 true] [17592186372605 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535885 true] [17592186372605 1111 #uuid "fc09e4cc-7d0a-5fed-8738-20dec76df9f1" 13194139535885 true] [17592186372606 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535885 true] [17592186372606 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535885 true] [17592186372606 1111 #uuid "123f649c-dde0-556d-91ce-d94189a1a884" 13194139535885 true] [17592186372607 1034 "II only" 13194139535885 true] [17592186372607 1103 #edb/ref 175921